{"archetypes":[{"name":"ci-harness","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Makefile shard wiring and harness catalog removal can silently break lint shard coverage or CI expectations.","prompt_body":"Investigate the Makefile changes that remove test-merge-parity from .PHONY, test-harnesses-5, and the standalone target. Check whether remaining harness shard coverage, py-test delegation, and docs/linting.md catalog wording stay consistent with how CI actually runs Python parity tests. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"trust-boundary-docs","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"SECURITY.md now makes detailed claims about report_tokens scan and issue redaction behavior that should match implementation.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the new SECURITY.md trust-boundary prose accurately describes python/report_tokens_scan.py, python/report_tokens_issue.py, and python/redact.py behavior. Pay particular attention to symlink skipping, invalid JSON handling, workflow unknown retention, repo slug and issue number validation, warning redaction, and single-pass issue-body redaction. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
